From: MacSW maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Act as the main process of an app bundle when asked to.

SOLIDWORKS.app (the MacSW launcher) re-executes its own executable as the Wine
loader, so the Wine host process is that bundle's process: LaunchServices
shows one Dock tile with the bundle's name and icon and sends the bundle's
Apple events to it. The launcher sets MACSW_APP_BUNDLE to its bundle path.
winemac honours the variables below only in the process whose main bundle is
that path (realpath of both). Wine processes that the host starts inherit the
variables, but they run MacSW.app's loader, whose main bundle is another
directory, so nothing changes for them. The variables are read once.

MACSW_APP_BUNDLE=<bundle path>: the bundle's Info.plist makes the process a
regular app from launch (Dock tile while starting), so the one-time setup in
transformProcessToForeground (menu, App Nap activity, icon) also runs once
when the policy is already regular. The Quit menu item uses Command-Q, not
Command-Option-Q.

MACSW_OPEN_DOCUMENTS_HELPER=<program>: documents opened from Finder, the
Dock or "open -a" (kAEOpenDocuments, at launch and while running) are passed
as "<program> --open-documents <path>..." to that program, which hands them
to the running Windows application. The helper is started with its native
slice preferred, no inherited descriptors except stdout/stderr and default
signal state. Otherwise the delegate reports that it does not implement
-application:openURLs:, so AppKit behaves as before.

MACSW_APP_QUIT=close: Quit (Command-Q, the Dock, the menu) posts WM_CLOSE to
every top-level window of the process, as taskkill without /f does, and
cancels the termination; the program asks to save and exits by itself. Log
out, restart and shut down keep Wine's session-end path. Without the
variable, Quit keeps Wine's path (WM_QUERYENDSESSION, WM_ENDSESSION, then
the process ends).

Outside that process nothing changes.
